feat(tool-market): audit_energy_decay — test his one quantified claim

'breaks release their strongest energy within 5-10 bars, rarely beyond' is the
only part of the method stated numerically, so it is the only part we can falsify.
The tool finds confirmed fractal swings, takes the first bar that CLOSES beyond
one, measures where the favourable excursion peaks over a fixed horizon, and
reports the distribution with its blind spots.

On 10 years of daily data the claim does not survive, on four commodities:

  GC=F  379 breaks: 21.4% peak inside bars 5-10, 44.6% after bar 10, median 9
  SI=F  437 breaks: 18.3% inside 5-10, 42.3% after 10, median 8
  CL=F  438 breaks: 20.5% inside 5-10, 44.7% after 10, median 9
  HG=F  447 breaks: 17.0% inside 5-10, 45.6% after 10, median 9

So the narrow window is wrong in both directions, while the loose shape (median
peak around bar 9, i.e. energy concentrates early) survives. Reporting that split
is the point of the tool: it is evidence, not agreement.

The verdict rule had to change once real data arrived: a sample that contradicts
both halves of a claim is NOT_SUPPORTED, not NOT_PROVEN — absence of evidence and
evidence against are different answers.

Tri-state, deterministic, and it still refuses to conclude under 30 events.
34 test files, 548 tests.